  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are the thermal conductivities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are the lengths and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are the cross sectional areas of steel and copper rods respectively such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Then, for the arrangement as shown in the figure. The value of temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> of the steel - copper junction in the steady state will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3cf8a2db-465a-4488-a57c-69225a356d00-image.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 137px;\" /></p>",
